menu "CDC2NET"

choice CDC2NET_SOURCE
    prompt "Bridge data source"
    default CDC2NET_SOURCE_USB
    help
        Selects the single data source the bridge fans out to the TCP sink(s).
        Each board/mission builds exactly ONE source (see docs/merge-targets.md
        for the Board x Mission matrix).  v0.1 ships USB only; the UART
        (EUL/TUL serial-downlink stick) and Thread/RCP sources are added as
        sibling options here when their merge milestones land.

config CDC2NET_SOURCE_USB
    bool "USB host (CDC-ACM + FTDI/CH34x/CP210x VCP)"
    help
        USB-OTG host port opens the attached stick: native CDC-ACM
        (CUL/TUL/EUL), or a foreign FTDI / WCH CH34x / Silabs CP210x
        USB-serial bridge through its VCP driver (chip framing + baud).
        Requires a USB-OTG-capable SoC (ESP32-S2 / S3 / P4).

config CDC2NET_SOURCE_UART
    bool "Onboard radio over hardware UART (EUL/TUL serial downlink)"
    help
        The EUL/TUL sticks carry their radio module (EnOcean TCM515 on
        EUL) on an internal hardware UART instead of a USB-host port.
        Byte-transparent pipe: UART RX -> bridge -> TCP, and back; the
        host (FHEM) speaks ESP3 to the TCM515 end-to-end through the pipe.
        Works on any SoC with a spare UART (the EUL/TUL line is C3/C6/C5).
        Pins/baud default to the C6 EUL generation; override via -D flags.

endchoice

config CDC2NET_ETH_W5500
    bool "W5500 SPI Ethernet (FPC add-on, line-wide on the C6 generation)"
    default n
    help
        Bring up a Wiznet W5500 SPI Ethernet PHY in addition to / instead
        of WiFi.  The C6 EUL/TUL generation has an FPC header for a W5500.
        Coexists with the WiFi-STA/SoftAP net layer (the TCP listener binds
        INADDR_ANY and serves over whichever interface has an IP).  Probed
        at boot: absent W5500 -> logged and skipped, WiFi still comes up.
        SPI pins default to the EULFW32 C6 map; override via -D flags.

config CDC2NET_EEPROM_M24C32
    bool "M24C32 I2C config EEPROM (EUL/TUL C6 carrier)"
    default n
    help
        Probe an M24C32 32-Kbit I2C serial EEPROM (slave 0x50) at boot and
        run a non-destructive read-modify-write self-test, surfacing the
        result + geometry as the WebUI "EEPROM" tile (features.eeprom + the
        eeprom{} status block).  The C6 EUL/TUL generation carries this part
        on a dedicated WE-gated I2C bus; the shared bridge PCB leaves the pads
        unpopulated, so leave this off there (the tile stays hidden).  A
        missing/broken chip is handled gracefully (state 0/2), never asserts.
        Pins default to the EULFW32 C6 map (SDA=22 SCL=23 WE=15); override -D.

config CDC2NET_MISSION_TBR
    bool "Experimental: on-device Thread Border Router (C6 native radio + W5500 backbone)"
    default n
    depends on CDC2NET_ETH_W5500
    help
        Bring up a full on-device OpenThread Border Router on the ESP32-C6's
        native 802.15.4 radio, using the W5500 ethernet netif as the IP backbone,
        running alongside the UART-source bridge — a single C6 stick acting as
        both a serial bridge and a Thread border router (no RCP / second radio).
        Requires CONFIG_CDC2NET_ETH_W5500.  Pulls in OpenThread + full lwIP IPv6
        forwarding + mbedtls ECJPAKE/DTLS — append sdkconfig.defaults.tbr to the
        build's SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS for the matching Kconfig values.  Experimental.

endmenu
